# Code style

Import order: Next.js, React, third-party, local components, constants.

Components are default-exported functions.

```tsx
export default function About() {
  return (
    <>
      <section className="mt-24 px-[4.5rem] md:px-[8vw]">...</section>
    </>
  );
}
```

- Simple props are inline. Complex props use an `interface`. Never `any`.
- Multiple roots use `<>...</>`. Do not add a wrapper `div` only to group sections.
- Responsive visibility is `hidden md:block` or `block md:hidden`. Do not branch layout on an `isMobile` flag.
- Lists use a stable id as `key`. An index is allowed only when the list is static and never reordered.

## Images

Always `next/image`, with `alt`, and `width`/`height` or `fill`.

```tsx
<Image src="/logo.png" alt="Glamsfyt logo" width={405} height={286} className="w-[25.313rem]" />
```

## Navigation

Prefer `<Link>` over `router.push`. A CTA that opens another page is a `<Link>` styled as a button. Do not nest a `<button>` inside a `<Link>`.

```tsx
<Link href="/solutions" className="mt-8 inline-block rounded-2xl bg-[#FCC010] px-[3.75rem] py-[1.125rem] text-black">
  Learn More
</Link>
```

A page that already wraps a `<button>` in `<Link>` stays that way until the task is to change that control. New CTAs use the styled `Link`. A `<button type="button">` is for an action that does not navigate.
